A||N||6||Dan87GT||Stripped Exhaust Manifold Bolt||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||06-20-2001||07:32 AM||||I am going to fix my rear exhaust manifold leak again this weekend. I stripped out one of the bolt holes on the head, any ideas what size I should drill and re-tap the hole?? Of course it the one above the AC compressor........||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||06-20-2001||08:16 AM||||I have no real experience in this area, but...<P>FYI - The 8mm tapped hole in the head, is just a <B>touch</B> larger in diameter than 5/16 inch.  So you'll have to go bigger than that - I'd probably think about using a 3/8" stud or bolt.        <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000002||Dan87GT||06-20-2001||11:03 AM||||Some of the threads are there but no enough for any good grip. Can I go ahead and re-tap with a 5/16"? Any thoughts?||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||06-20-2001||11:57 AM||||I was able to repair two cars by just putting a longer bolt than the original bolt.  The hole is a lot deeper than the original bolt so the thread are only stripped partway down the hole.  Good luck.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Toddster||06-20-2001||07:29 PM||||I haven't had to do it but I have a spare engine in the garage. I just took a few width measurements and 3/8 looks like it will cler just fine. Be sure to drill out the hole in your manifold too. <P>One tip, start the tapping process with a 3/8 bolt flush to the head so the tap goes in straight.<p>[This message has been edited by Toddster (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||06-21-2001||02:46 AM||||I would either use a longer stud or I would use a 5/16 helicoil and a stud. Use a stud when ever you do manifold work. It makes things in the future so much nicer.,||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||06-21-2001||09:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Toddster:<BR><B>One tip, start the tapping process with a 3/8 bolt flush to the head so the tap goes in straight.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <BR>Okay, I'm confused - did you really mean use a 3/8 <B>nut</B> to guide the tap?  Just looking for clarification  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>When it comes to "nuts" and "holes in the head," you'd think I'd know all about those subjects  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <BR>||||reg||5
